\section{Conclusions}
We presented a thyroid nodule segmentation pipeline based on DeepLabV3+ with an EfficientNet-B5 backbone, including an ablation study across three different channel-attention modules (SE, CBAM, GCA), two loss formulations (Dice-BCE and Boundary) and a split conformal prediction layer for pixel-level uncertainty quantification.
The plain backbone already matches previously reported results on TN3K, while the additional attention modules provide only marginal, non-monotonic gains: no module dominates across the four Dice variants, the two MCC aggregations and the five detection rates we report.
The conformal layer concentrates the uncertainty along the nodule boundary, aligning the model's confidence with the inter-observer variability intrinsic to the task.
The main limitation is the use of a single dataset.
Future work will extend the pipeline to malignancy classification and metastatic-risk prediction.
