\subsection{Inference and Prediction}
\label{subsec:models}
Inference was performed on a single NVIDIA A100 GPU with 80~GB of VRAM using Ollama version 0.35.1 as the inference engine, with FP16 precision configured. The observed GPU memory usage was 22,364~MiB for CLEF (27B) and 13,741~MiB for CLEF-Flash (9B). Each request contained the Base64-encoded original image and the corresponding prompt and decision schema.
For each image, a single classification question is defined using the \texttt{choice} decision type. The available choices correspond exactly to the diagnostic labels of the evaluated dataset. The model returns a probability for each allowed category, and the category with the highest probability is taken as the predicted class.
\begin{equation}
\hat{y} = \arg\max_{c \in C} P(c \mid I, P),
\end{equation}
where $I$ denotes the input ultrasound image, $P$ represents the prompting strategy, and $C$ denotes the set of diagnostic categories.
