\subsection*{Experimental Protocol}
\begin{enumerate}
 \item \textbf{Base VLM evaluation:} Each backbone is first evaluated in a query-only setting on the held-out test split.
 \item \textbf{ARISE evaluation:} The same backbone is evaluated on the same query split after the five-stage ARISE workflow constructs the verified hypothesis state $H^*$.
 \item \textbf{Task-level comparison:} Accuracy, F1 score, precision, and recall are reported for Base and ARISE on all four clinical tasks.
 \item \textbf{Stage-level analysis:} Scores S1--S5 are compared across the four VLMs on the Crohn's disease six-lesion classification task. S3 is computed on a separate 50-example validation subset.
 \item \textbf{Process vs. outcome analysis:} The weighted AGENTIC score is compared with the TASK score to identify cases in which a well-formed reasoning process does not fully translate to correct final classification.
\end{enumerate}
